  {
   "bbox": [
    300.48,
    78.0,
    537.6,
    234.48
   ],
   "id": "e19",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      78.0,
      456.96,
      86.64
     ],
     "text": "Morphology — see comparison tables."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      87.84,
      519.12,
      96.48
     ],
     "text": "‘Autumn Blue’ is a compact, upright, herbaceous plant"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      97.92,
      507.6,
      106.8
     ],
     "text": "which flowers during autumn, winter and spring. In"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      108.0,
      516.96,
      116.64
     ],
     "text": "comparison, the blue form of Leehenauitia biloba, and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      301.2,
      118.08,
      532.08,
      126.72
     ],
     "text": "‘White Flash’, flower only in spring. ‘Autumn Blue’ leaves"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.72,
      127.68,
      527.04,
      136.32
     ],
     "text": "are the same width as the comparative varieties, but are"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.72,
      137.76,
      533.04,
      145.2
     ],
     "text": "shorter than those of ‘White Flash’. ‘Autumn Blue’ has an"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      301.2,
      147.6,
      530.16,
      156.72
     ],
     "text": "upright growth habit in contrast to the semi-erect growth"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      301.2,
      157.44,
      530.16,
      166.08
     ],
     "text": "habit of the comparative varieties. ‘Autumn Blue’ flowers"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.72,
      167.04,
      535.2,
      175.44
     ],
     "text": "are narrower in diameter and shorter in height and corolla"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      177.12,
      528.96,
      185.76
     ],
     "text": "length than the comparative varieties. The newly opened"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.72,
      187.2,
      521.04,
      195.36
     ],
     "text": "flowers of ‘Autumn Blue’ are slightly darker violet-blue"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      197.04,
      519.36,
      205.68
     ],
     "text": "than the comparative varieties, and when fully opened"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.72,
      206.88,
      513.84,
      215.76
     ],
     "text": "they are blue. The aged flowers of ‘Autumn Blue’ are"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.72,
      216.72,
      537.6,
      224.64
     ],
     "text": "violet-blue, whereas those of the blue form of Z. biloba and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      301.44,
      227.52,
      390.24,
      234.48
     ],
     "text": "‘White Flash’ are blue."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Morphology — see comparison tables.\n‘Autumn Blue’ is a compact, upright, herbaceous plant\nwhich flowers during autumn, winter and spring. In\ncomparison, the blue form of Leehenauitia biloba, and\n‘White Flash’, flower only in spring. ‘Autumn Blue’ leaves\nare the same width as the comparative varieties, but are\nshorter than those of ‘White Flash’. ‘Autumn Blue’ has an\nupright growth habit in contrast to the semi-erect growth\nhabit of the comparative varieties. ‘Autumn Blue’ flowers\nare narrower in diameter and shorter in height and corolla\nlength than the comparative varieties. The newly opened\nflowers of ‘Autumn Blue’ are slightly darker violet-blue\nthan the comparative varieties, and when fully opened\nthey are blue. The aged flowers of ‘Autumn Blue’ are\nviolet-blue, whereas those of the blue form of Z. biloba and\n‘White Flash’ are blue.",
   "text_format": "plain",
